    "result_text": "All 23 tests pass, including `Cp14Tests` (the membership-number test). BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is fully derivable from the owner's existing fields, I followed the same pattern already used for `displayName` and `initials` \u2014 a computed mapping rather than a stored column:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema (this generates the `membershipNumber` accessor on `OwnerDto` at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   `year % 100` with `%02d` correctly zero-pads (e.g. 2026 \u2192 `26`, 2007 \u2192 `07`), matching the test's `registrationDate.substring(2,4)` expectation. Both `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are always populated by the controller before the mapper runs, so the derivation is always well-defined.",
